# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Reader data written at runtime (reactions, push subscriptions).
# On the VPS this lives in DATA_DIR outside the repo instead.
.data/

# The SQLite file docs/running-locally.md tells you to make:
#   export DATABASE_URL="file:./.local-dev.db"
# Three files, in the repository root, that nothing ignored — so every agent
# who followed that page left them untracked in the shared checkout, where
# they read as somebody's uncommitted work and get in the way of the next
# `git merge`. Found on 2026-09-05 with all three sitting on `main`.
.local-dev.db
.local-dev.db-*

# Local development artefacts.
# `/mail` is where signup mail used to land, from a `process.cwd()` fallback
# that B111 removed. Still ignored so an old checkout's plaintext codes cannot
# be committed by somebody who has not cleared the directory out yet.
/mail

# Agent worktrees and local agent state — but .claude/skills/ is part of the
# repository. The skills are how an agent is told to do the things the author
# actually does (ROADMAP G1); they are source, not local state.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
# One exception in the other direction: this instance's own deploy path — its
# host, its ssh alias, its one command. The shipped software's deploy is
# scripts/deploy.sh and the `deploy` skill, which work on anybody's VPS; a
# skill that hardcodes ours is local state wearing a skill's clothes.
.claude/skills/vps/

# What scripts/deploy.sh last brought up healthy, written on the server (B258).
.deploy-state

# Generated per-user output. Postcards carry postal addresses, so none of it
# belongs in git — with content/example the deliberate exception, since it
# holds nothing real.
content/*/postcards/
content/*/photobooks/
# Sent mail lived here before B636 moved it to `<dataDir>/mail/`, which
# `.data/` above already covers. Still ignored so a checkout that has not
# restarted since, or has not cleared the old directory by hand, cannot
# accidentally commit a plaintext sign-in code.
content/*/mail/
content/.mail/
# The files exactly as the camera wrote them. Kept so the photobook has
# something better than a 2000px derivative to print from, gitignored because
# a repository is the wrong place for a hundred 40 MB originals.
content/*/trips/*/originals/
!content/example/

# scratch output from .claude/skills/apply-the-brand/favicon-check.mjs
favicon-check.png

# Playwright MCP scratch output (screenshots, snapshots, console logs)
.playwright-mcp/

# Journal exports. `npm run export` writes real content — somebody's actual
# trips, photographs and addresses — and it must never be committed.
*-export.zip
/*.png

# Resized copies made by the media route, rebuilt on demand.
content/.cache/

# Tombstones for deleted journals and trips (lib/tombstones.ts). They keep the
# username reserved and make old URLs answer 410, and they name real people's
# journals — so they live on the operator's disk, not in the repository.
content/.deleted/

# B1064's registry lock — one journal per proven email, one per proven
# number (lib/registry.ts). Rebuildable from content/ with
# `npm run registry -- reconcile`, and it names real addresses and numbers.
content/.registry/

# Journal backups from `npm run export`. Never committed: they hold private
# trips and unpublished drafts.
exports/

# Alternative build outputs — see NEXT_DIST_DIR in next.config.ts.
.next-*

# Downloaded Natural Earth sources for scripts/build-mapdata.mjs — the baked
# output in lib/mapdata/ is committed, these are not.
.mapdata-cache/
.qa-shots/

# The ECB reference rates are a measurement with a date on them, refreshed
# nightly on the server into DATA_DIR — instance state, not source (B1084).
# They were committed here until then, and this entry is what stops a stray
# `npm run rates:update` on somebody's laptop putting them back: a table that
# arrives by `git pull` is one that only moves when a person deploys, which is
# the bug.
site/rates/

